{"schema_version":"1","crate":"blinkenlights","version":"0.4.0","id":"15109cb3af7adbcb","name":"BBS.Sim_CPU.io.tape.tm11","qualified_name":"BBS.Sim_CPU.io.tape.tm11","kind":"ada_package","location":{"file":"../../../home/runner/.local/share/alire/builds/bbs_simcpu_0.6.0_d74538a6/9cdc441e7ff3f33fced7ac7acaa0da633fb83bcec604d59dd89b3ca09151f539/src/io/bbs-sim_cpu-io-tape-tm11.ads","line":25,"column":9},"code":"package BBS.Sim_CPU.io.tape.tm11","documentation":{"description":"\n----------------------------------------------------------------------\nThis is an I/O device for a TM11 magnetic tape controller.  It is\ndesigned to work with the PDP-11 simulations.\n\nThe device object for a TM11.\n\nNote that while this is a tape drive, it has more in common with disks than\nit does with paper tapes.\n\nFor compatibility with simh produced tapes, the following from simh pdp11_tm.c\nis followed:\n Magnetic tapes are represented as a series of variable 8b records\n of the form:\n\n   32b record length in bytes - exact number\n   byte 0\n   byte 1\n   :\n   byte n-2\n   byte n-1\n   32b record length in bytes - exact number\n\nIf the byte count is odd, the record is padded with an extra byte\nof junk.  File marks are represented by a single record length of 0.\nEnd of tape is two consecutive end of file marks."},"tagged_types":[{"id":"f333b8a604bd767d","name":"tm11","qualified_name":"BBS.Sim_CPU.io.tape.tm11.tm11","kind":"ada_tagged_type","location":{"file":"../../../home/runner/.local/share/alire/builds/bbs_simcpu_0.6.0_d74538a6/9cdc441e7ff3f33fced7ac7acaa0da633fb83bcec604d59dd89b3ca09151f539/src/io/bbs-sim_cpu-io-tape-tm11.ads","line":53,"column":9},"code":"type tm11 is new mtape with private;","documentation":{"description":"\n\nI/O device actions\n\nWrite to a port address"},"parent_type":{"qualified_name":"BBS.Sim_CPU.io.tape.mtape","id":"9b8dabcd427178a0","unit":"bbs-sim_cpu-io-tape"},"dispatching_declared":[{"qualified_name":"BBS.Sim_CPU.io.tape.tm11.extend","id":"ab261